              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "dependencies",
                  "known_vulnerable_component"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.0"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OSV.dev reports GHSA-7gcf-g7xr-8hxj for crates.io package serde_with at version 3.12.0: serde_with: KeyValueMap serialization panics on empty sequence or map entries. The advisory names no affected functions, so reachability was not determined. Upgrade to a fixed version (3.21.0). Advisory data comes from OSV.dev at the recorded time. Reachability is judged from names, not a call graph: the affected functions the advisory lists against the identifiers in the audited product code, a Cargo feature it says is off by default against the audited manifests, the platforms it lists against the declared Rust targets. Indirect calls (traits, macros, other dependencies) are not followed."
